  "title": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR rupee (8.11g), Kashmir, VS1889",
  "description": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR rupee (8.11g), Kashmir, VS1889, KM-C50var, Herrli-—, reduced weight standard, final digit of date (\"9\") recut over \"8\", Extremely Fine, RRR.  The local governor of Kashmir, Shaik Gholam, circa VS1889-1891, reduced the weight of the rupee from the standard 10.8-11.0g to the range of 8.0-8.5g, for unknown reasons. Herrli lists two varieties, dated VS1890 (type 06-41-04) and VS1891 (type 06-42.04). Full weight rupees were restored late in VS1891.",
